    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0012" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34553B/72</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Portuguese Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Salazar</hi>)<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d2-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-07">January 7,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have today received a
                        telegram<anchor n="6" xml:id="d2-f2"/> from the Secretary of State
                    indicating that he, the Secretary of War,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d2-f3"/> and the
                    Secretary of the Navy<anchor n="8" xml:id="d2-f4"/> concur in the suggestion
                    that an American commercial company should conduct the survey of the Azores,
                    which we discussed on the last day of December. They are also in agreement that
                    Pan American Airways, Inc. is the best equipped commercial organization to
                    undertake this task. That Company has been informally and confidentially
                    consulted and its acceptance obtained in advance should it be selected to do
                    this work.</p>
                <p>I thought that it might prove a convenience to you if I sent you this information
                    in writing. At the same time, I wish to ask for an appointment to see you at
                    your earliest convenience.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d2-f1" n="5" type="source" xml:id="d2-f1-content">
